# Forest wolf (#331, D115): native 48x24 frames, facing right, feet on row 23. A lean, low-slung wolf on long legs, long
# muzzle, pricked ears, brush tail; drawn about 20 px tall and 38 px long, the largest Forest monster. Near legs in dusty rose
# (l, L), far legs dark (d) behind them.
# stand: idle; trot1, trot2: the patrol trot (trot1 head lowest, held for the sniff); alert, hackle, scrape: the notice (head
# up, then front dropped with the spiky ridge p, then a forepaw drawn back); run1-run4: the gallop (gathered, extended and
# between, tail streaming, ears back); skid: braced, head turned back; crouch: the wind-up (rump high, jaws open, fangs f);
# lunge: stretched flat, 2 px off the floor; bite: head down, jaws shut; shake: the harmless recovery, head down and away;
# bay: half-sitting, open muzzle raised to the sky; dead: lying flat on its side along the floor, forelegs stretched forward
# under its flat head, hind legs back, tail limp (author, 2026-11-21: a wolf lies stretched out, its paws never stick up).
# Danger family (#236, author 2026-11-21): dark crimson pelt 86101f with shades 4a0c22 and 2a0612, rose lights 9c2050,
# b85a80, c87896, glowing eye ff6b57, legs 9a6070 and b07c8c; the moon rim comes from the exporter (D92).
